    "boat": {
      "word": "BOAT",
      "definitions": [
        {
          "text": "A small open vessel, or water craft, usually moved by cars or paddles, but often by a sail. wherry, pinnace, punt, etc.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "Hence, any vessel; usually with some epithet descriptive of its use or mode of propulsion; as, pilot boat, packet boat, passage boat, advice boat, etc. The term is sometimes applied to steam vessels, even of the largest class; as, the Cunard boats.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "A vehicle, utensil, or dish, somewhat resembling a boat in shape; as, a stone boat; a gravy boat. boat builder or boatbuilder; boat building or boatbuilding; boat hook or boathook; boathouse; boat keeper or boatkeeper; boat load; boat race; boat racing; boat rowing; boat song; boatlike; boat-shaped. Advice boat. See under Advice. to a long pole, to pull or push a boat, raft, log, etc. Totten. painter. F. W. Newman.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "To transport in a boat; as, to boat goods.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "To place in a boat; as, to boat oars. To boat the oars. See under Oar.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "To go or row in a boat. I boated over, ran my craft aground. Tennyson.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        }
      ],
